      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 39-year-old woman was evaluated for acute midepigastric pain. The patient was never severely ill; her only medication was an oral contraceptive (OC) which she took regularly over the last 12 years. Abdominal ultrasonography and computed tomography revealed bleeding into a liver tumor. At laparoscopy, 3 adenomas of the liver were detected. Bleeding was restricted to 1 tumor and did not require surgical intervention. OC medication was discontinued, and the patient was followed over more than 3 years. The patient was doing very well; ultrasonographically, the liver tumors became gradually smaller."},
